    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d668">

                <pb facs="0791" n="1625" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/280</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-23T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 25, 12.12 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3439. For War Trade Board [from Heck]:</p>
                <p>No. 46. Our No. 45.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d668-f1"/> German-Swiss convention
                    covering period of nine months from May 1 signed May 22. It may be denounced
                    every second month by a preliminary notice of one month. It contains no clause
                    referring to deliveries of coal by countries at war with Germany. Heck.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
